  data: {
    LLM: '1. Players draw lottery sticks to determine partnerships.\n2. Trump (Kiri) is determined by a cut or rotation.\n3. Must follow suit if possible; if not, any card can be played.\n4. **Scoring**: Only Face cards (16 total) matter. Winning 9-11 = 1 stone, 12-15 = 2 stones, 16 (All) = 4 stones.',
    Player: '1. Players draw lottery sticks to determine partnerships.\n2. Trump (Kiri) is determined by a cut or rotation.\n3. Must follow suit if possible; if not, any card can be played.\n4. **Scoring**: Only Face cards (16 total) matter. Winning 9-11 = 1 stone, 12-15 = 2 stones, 16 (All) = 4 stones.',
    objective: "Win 'Face Cards' (J-Q-K-A) in tricks. The team that captures 9 or more of the 16 face cards wins a Go stone from their opponents.",
    gameplay: '1. Players draw lottery sticks to determine partnerships.\n2. Trump (Kiri) is determined by a cut or rotation.\n3. Must follow suit if possible; if not, any card can be played.\n4. **Scoring**: Only Face cards (16 total) matter. Winning 9-11 = 1 stone, 12-15 = 2 stones, 16 (All) = 4 stones.',
    keyRules: [
      'The Rensho (usually Ace of Spades) is the highest card and wins any trick it is played to',
